From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi: advertise the bsta-mld driver-name token

The default driver matches interfaces by name token. Without "bsta-mld" in
that list a backhaul STA MLD interface finds no driver, so wifi.bstamld is
never published and the whole bSTA-MLD chain stops before it starts.

Companion to the map-agent and map-controller backhaul MLD patches. Rescued
from the 2026-07-16 control-plane work (tag backhaul-mld-controlplane-2026-07-16)
and re-applied to the current tree on 2026-07-22.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
+++ b/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
@@ -2187,7 +2187,7 @@
 
 
 const struct wifi_driver default_wifi_driver = {
-	.name = "wlan,phy,bsta,ap-mld",
+	.name = "wlan,phy,bsta,ap-mld,bsta-mld",
 	.info = nlwifi_driver_info,
 
 	/* Radio/phy callbacks */
